 # Stream C notes
 
 ## How it works (plain language)
-- TBD
+- **One request, one pipeline.** `POST /api/search` → `backend/app/services/pipeline.py::run_search`:
+  1. Read the photo (base64 or a URL), fix phone rotation (EXIF).
+  2. `detect.py` finds boxes (or, by default, none: we use the user's box or the whole image) and crops with 5% padding.
+  3. `serp.py` sends the crop to **Google Lens** (upload flow: we shrink it under SerpApi's 500 KB limit, upload, get an `image_id`, then search).
+  4. We take Lens's top title, add the user's refinement text ("yellow version"), and search **Google Shopping**.
+  5. Candidates from both lists are merged and de-duplicated by link.
+  6. `images.py` downloads every candidate image **in parallel** (full-size first, thumbnail if that fails).
+  7. Stream A's matcher scores each image against our crop → `identical / similar / none`.
+  8. `ranking.py` (contract C7) builds the three top-3 lists from identical/similar USD-priced items.
+- **Caching protects our quota.** Every SerpApi answer is saved raw to `backend/app/cache/<sha256>.json`
+  (contract C4). Asking the same thing twice costs 0 searches. Candidate images are cached on disk too.
+- **Cached demo mode.** `DEMO_CACHED=true` → never touch the network. If a query or image wasn't cached,
+  the API returns `503 cache_miss` instead of hanging. Run every demo object once live, then flip it on.
+- **Refinements are cheap.** Same photo + new text reuses the cached Lens result; only Shopping is re-run (1 search).
+- **Quota log.** Every real call is appended to `backend/app/cache/quota_log.jsonl`; `GET /api/quota` shows the counts.
+- **Safe URL fetching.** Only http(s); private/local addresses are blocked (re-checked on redirects);
+  5 s timeout and an 8 MB cap per image, so a user-supplied URL can't make the server read internal services.
 
 ## Key decisions
-- TBD
+- Cache keys: Lens upload = sha256(crop JPEG bytes + "google_lens"); Lens URL = the URL's bytes stand in for
+  image bytes; Shopping = sha256("" + "google_shopping" + query text).
+- Searches per new query: 1 Lens + 1 Shopping (+ 1 upload, which may or may not count; check on the SerpApi dashboard).
+- Only USD prices enter the ranking pool. Other currencies are shown but not ranked.
+- A candidate whose image can't be downloaded gets score 0 / `none` (shown, never ranked).
+- Used/refurbished condition goes in `description` (answers Sid's new-vs-used question without a contract change).
+- Ranking interpretations (ties, null ratings, median) are listed at the top of
+  `backend/tests/data/ranking_test_vectors.proposed.json`.
+
+## Needs team approval (bring to the Saturday 6 PM call)
+1. **Ranking test vectors.** 12 cases in `backend/tests/data/ranking_test_vectors.proposed.json`. Once the team
+   approves (incl. Shrihan, who must match them in `ranking.ts`), copy `cases` into `shared/ranking_test_vectors.json`.
+2. **Error codes for D** (add to `docs/contracts.md` C1): `400 bad_image`, `503 cache_miss`, `503 quota_exhausted`,
+   `503 no_api_key`, `502 upstream_error`; body `{"detail": {"code", "message"}}`. Shrihan can build error states on these.
+3. **decisions.md (CP1):** detector = fallback (`DETECTOR=none`) unless the YOLO spike looks good; crop padding 5%;
+   ranking m = pool median review count (min 1), C = pool mean, w = 0.5.
+4. **Price-outlier rule** (suggestion 4): not implemented, since it changes the C7 spec. Decide before both sides code it.
+5. **Shrihan's new fields** (`suggestions`, `reviews_scanned`) need a `schemas.py` change; not done.
+
+## Not done yet (later Stream C work)
+- Stage 1a/1b runs: need your SerpApi key and photos (see "How to run" below). Put the numbers in decisions.md.
+- 7e reviews: `reviews.trust_rating` works (helpfulness-weighted mean) but review fetching isn't wired in.
+  Waiting on B's formula; likely uses SerpApi's `google_product` engine for the top 2–3 products only.
+- 4h hosting: `make serve` already serves the built frontend; tunnel: `cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:8000`.
+  HF Space backup still to do.
+- Swap in real models (Wed 12/2): nothing to change here; A edits `ml/inference/matcher.py`, B edits `ml/inference/reviews.py`.
+
+## How to run
+```bash
+cp .env.example .env          # put SERPAPI_KEY in .env
+make test                      # all offline
+python backend/scripts/spike_serp.py --image-file photo1.jpg --image-file photo2.jpg --out backend/scripts/spike_results.json
+USE_MOCK_RESPONSE=false make dev-backend
+curl -s localhost:8000/api/search -H 'content-type: application/json' \
+  -d "{\"image_base64\": \"$(base64 -w0 photo1.jpg)\"}" | head -c 600
+```
 
 ## What I'd say if a judge asks…
-- TBD
+- *"How do you avoid burning your API quota?"* Every response is cached by image hash + engine + text; repeats are free,
+  refinements reuse the Lens result, and we log every real call.
+- *"What if the Wi-Fi dies?"* `DEMO_CACHED=true` serves everything from disk, including candidate images.
+- *"Why not just trust Google Lens's order?"* Lens returns look-alikes. Our matcher re-scores each candidate's
+  full-size image against the user's crop and labels it identical/similar/none, and only those feed the rankings.
+- *"Why is a 4.6 ranked below a 4.4?"* Bayesian average: a 4.6 from 5 reviews is pulled toward the pool mean more than
+  a 4.4 from 5,000 reviews.
+- *"Is it safe to fetch arbitrary URLs?"* http(s) only, private/local IPs blocked on every redirect, timeouts and size caps.
